From: Orion Parker <331738732+orionparker33@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 04:57:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] cc253x/usb: ep_tx: do not overwrite a loaded IN FIFO

The CC253x IN endpoint FIFO is single buffered. If ep_tx() runs while the
previous packet is still waiting for the host (INPKT_RDY set), it used to
write the next packet over it. Leave the buffer queued instead; the IN
interrupt sends it once the host has collected the previous packet.
---
 cpu/cc253x/usb/usb-arch.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/cpu/cc253x/usb/usb-arch.c b/cpu/cc253x/usb/usb-arch.c
index ae7410d..74d18e3 100644
--- a/cpu/cc253x/usb/usb-arch.c
+++ b/cpu/cc253x/usb/usb-arch.c
@@ -1129,6 +1129,14 @@ ep_tx(uint8_t ep_hw)
     return 0;
   }
 
+  /*
+   * The IN FIFO is single buffered: if the previous packet has not been
+   * collected yet, keep the buffer queued. The IN interrupt sends it.
+   */
+  if(USBCSIL & USBCSIL_INPKT_RDY) {
+    return 0;
+  }
+
   while(ep->buffer) {
     unsigned int copy;
 
